{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"oracle-naming-scope-correction-2026-10-03","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Oracle naming scope correction — 2026-10-03"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reviewed implementation: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/commit/fe40ab59191d046bda12cc9563cdc4a82b5fd97c","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fe40ab59191d046bda12cc9563cdc4a82b5fd97c"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nClassification evidence refers to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"134b7e8bacce5999ab7e06da96d5dbe9989820f5"},{"type":"text","value":", before the reverse moves.\nThe "},{"type":"link","href":"2026-10-03-oracle-naming-scope.json","children":[{"type":"text","value":"classification ledger"}]},{"type":"text","value":" names each evidence path and its line numbers, final path, role, and naming decision."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"corrected-scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Corrected scope"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The earlier claim of 251 executable oracle owners and dedicated companions was too broad.\nThe audit category included ordinary examples, type assertions, harness tests, fixtures, and documentation.\nConverting that category directly into a rename list was incorrect.\nThis record supersedes the naming inventory in "},{"type":"link","href":"2026-10-02-glossary-alignment.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the original review"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nIts 39 terminology resolutions remain intact."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This correction restores 101 original filenames and their imports, commands, replay references, and current documentation links.\nThe PR retains 63 moves: 57 files that execute an independent oracle and six model, grammar, or checker definitions.\nEach retained move has a named mechanism and source evidence in the ledger.\nExisting filenames that already contained "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"oracle"},{"type":"text","value":" before this PR remain unchanged."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Role in the original 251-file review scope"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Executes an independent model, comparison, or generalized checker"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"121"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defines an independent model, checker, or its history grammar"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordinary example, regression, or concrete type-assertion tests"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"67"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drivers, fixtures, registration, or supporting declarations"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"34"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness, checker-calibration, or prototype tests"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"17"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are file roles within the previous inventory, not a count of distinct oracles across the repository.\nSeveral files execute the same model, and a mixed test file can contain multiple oracle mechanisms.\nThe classification is conservative for borderline cases. It does not declare all pre-existing oracle names correct."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"naming-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Naming evidence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A retained owner executes an independent expected-result computation, state model, differential comparison, metamorphic relation, or reusable law checker.\nA definition owns that model, checker, or its history grammar and names its receiving owner.\nRandom generation is not required. Fixed histories can execute an independent model, as the optimistic settlement histories do.\nOrdinary fixed assertions and parameterization alone are insufficient.\nCoverage-map entries and opening comments do not substitute for executable evidence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of restored names include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transactions.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query.test-d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", the framework "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conformance.test"},{"type":"text","value":" entrypoints, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"trace-runner.ts"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThey contain fixed assertions, registration/driver mechanics, or generic execution plumbing.\nExamples of retained names include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortedMap-oracle.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", which compares against native Map plus full sorting,\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"proxy-oracle.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", which contains a native-value differential callback model alongside ordinary examples.\nThe test-only no-peek candidate returns to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"no-peek.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"; the independent filter/sort/slice reference remains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model-oracle.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The contributor guidance now states this distinction and requires separate counts for owners, definitions, and support.\nIt does not add a CI linter or introduce new product contracts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"preservation-checks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preservation checks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An independent content comparison accounted for all 2,164 tracked files before final whitespace formatting.\nIt found 2,048 unchanged blobs, 114 files with mapped path-reference substitutions, and the two naming-policy documents.\nThe correction preserves glossary definitions, identifier/prose fixes, assertions, model rules, and campaign inputs.\nFinal formatting changes only whitespace around shortened paths."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static checks found all 101 restored paths and all 251 classified files present and indexed.\nThey checked 672 relative imports, 68 explicit command paths, five browser script entries, and 42 replay targets.\nReplay title selectors remained valid. No stale restored-name references or escaped filename patterns remained in current files.\nHistorical review records and immutable revision links retain their original paths."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation-after-the-correction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation after the correction"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime check"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DB"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7,962"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"210"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"IVM"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"704"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"44"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Offline"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"242"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"18"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SQLite core"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"375"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node SQLite"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"109"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser SQLite"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"242"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electron SQLite"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"97"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"629"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"13"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query DB affected no-peek suites"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"18"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Angular receiving suites"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"290"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Total"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10,668"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"322"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SQLite core also reports one todo. Scoped ESLint passed for 166 changed TypeScript files.\nFormatting and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff --check"},{"type":"text","value":" passed.\nThese runs used the same installed dependencies described in the original record, with coverage and integrated typechecking disabled.\nThe direct command was "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node <installed-vitest>/vitest.mjs run --coverage.enabled=false --typecheck.enabled=false --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot"},{"type":"text","value":".\nDB used two workers. Framework and Query DB checks selected only the affected receiving files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The earlier locked-dependency, integrated-typecheck, and intermittent Query DB baseline limits remain.\nThis correction did not rerun the full Query DB package, package builds, or external-provider/native-host E2E campaigns.\nNo new typecheck or real-host claim follows from the runtime passes."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"oracle-naming-scope-correction-2026-10-03","text":"Oracle naming scope correction — 2026-10-03","level":1},{"id":"corrected-scope","text":"Corrected scope","level":2},{"id":"naming-evidence","text":"Naming evidence","level":2},{"id":"preservation-checks","text":"Preservation checks","level":2},{"id":"validation-after-the-correction","text":"Validation after the correction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Oracle naming scope correction — 2026-10-03\n\nReviewed implementation: [fe40ab59191d046bda12cc9563cdc4a82b5fd97c](https://github.com/TanStack/db/commit/fe40ab59191d046bda12cc9563cdc4a82b5fd97c).\nClassification evidence refers to `134b7e8bacce5999ab7e06da96d5dbe9989820f5`, before the reverse moves.\nThe [classification ledger](2026-10-03-oracle-naming-scope.json) names each evidence path and its line numbers, final path, role, and naming decision.\n\n## Corrected scope\n\nThe earlier claim of 251 executable oracle owners and dedicated companions was too broad.\nThe audit category included ordinary examples, type assertions, harness tests, fixtures, and documentation.\nConverting that category directly into a rename list was incorrect.\nThis record supersedes the naming inventory in [the original review](2026-10-02-glossary-alignment.md).\nIts 39 terminology resolutions remain intact.\n\nThis correction restores 101 original filenames and their imports, commands, replay references, and current documentation links.\nThe PR retains 63 moves: 57 files that execute an independent oracle and six model, grammar, or checker definitions.\nEach retained move has a named mechanism and source evidence in the ledger.\nExisting filenames that already contained `oracle` before this PR remain unchanged.\n\n| Role in the original 251-file review scope | Files |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Executes an independent model, comparison, or generalized checker | 121 |\n| Defines an independent model, checker, or its history grammar | 10 |\n| Ordinary example, regression, or concrete type-assertion tests | 67 |\n| Drivers, fixtures, registration, or supporting declarations | 34 |\n| Harness, checker-calibration, or prototype tests | 17 |\n| Documentation | 2 |\n\nThese are file roles within the previous inventory, not a count of distinct oracles across the repository.\nSeveral files execute the same model, and a mixed test file can contain multiple oracle mechanisms.\nThe classification is conservative for borderline cases. It does not declare all pre-existing oracle names correct.\n\n## Naming evidence\n\nA retained owner executes an independent expected-result computation, state model, differential comparison, metamorphic relation, or reusable law checker.\nA definition owns that model, checker, or its history grammar and names its receiving owner.\nRandom generation is not required. Fixed histories can execute an independent model, as the optimistic settlement histories do.\nOrdinary fixed assertions and parameterization alone are insufficient.\nCoverage-map entries and opening comments do not substitute for executable evidence.\n\nExamples of restored names include `transactions.test.ts`, `query.test-d.ts`, the framework `conformance.test` entrypoints, and `trace-runner.ts`.\nThey contain fixed assertions, registration/driver mechanics, or generic execution plumbing.\nExamples of retained names include `SortedMap-oracle.test.ts`, which compares against native Map plus full sorting,\nand `proxy-oracle.test.ts`, which contains a native-value differential callback model alongside ordinary examples.\nThe test-only no-peek candidate returns to `no-peek.ts`; the independent filter/sort/slice reference remains `model-oracle.ts`.\n\nThe contributor guidance now states this distinction and requires separate counts for owners, definitions, and support.\nIt does not add a CI linter or introduce new product contracts.\n\n## Preservation checks\n\nAn independent content comparison accounted for all 2,164 tracked files before final whitespace formatting.\nIt found 2,048 unchanged blobs, 114 files with mapped path-reference substitutions, and the two naming-policy documents.\nThe correction preserves glossary definitions, identifier/prose fixes, assertions, model rules, and campaign inputs.\nFinal formatting changes only whitespace around shortened paths.\n\nStatic checks found all 101 restored paths and all 251 classified files present and indexed.\nThey checked 672 relative imports, 68 explicit command paths, five browser script entries, and 42 replay targets.\nReplay title selectors remained valid. No stale restored-name references or escaped filename patterns remained in current files.\nHistorical review records and immutable revision links retain their original paths.\n\n## Validation after the correction\n\n| Runtime check | Passed | Files |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| DB | 7,962 | 210 |\n| IVM | 704 | 44 |\n| Offline | 242 | 18 |\n| SQLite core | 375 | 9 |\n| Node SQLite | 109 | 5 |\n| Browser SQLite | 242 | 9 |\n| Electron SQLite | 97 | 3 |\n| Electric | 629 | 13 |\n| Query DB affected no-peek suites | 18 | 2 |\n| React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Angular receiving suites | 290 | 9 |\n| Total | 10,668 | 322 |\n\nSQLite core also reports one todo. Scoped ESLint passed for 166 changed TypeScript files.\nFormatting and `git diff --check` passed.\nThese runs used the same installed dependencies described in the original record, with coverage and integrated typechecking disabled.\nThe direct command was `node <installed-vitest>/vitest.mjs run --coverage.enabled=false --typecheck.enabled=false --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot`.\nDB used two workers. Framework and Query DB checks selected only the affected receiving files.\n\nThe earlier locked-dependency, integrated-typecheck, and intermittent Query DB baseline limits remain.\nThis correction did not rerun the full Query DB package, package builds, or external-provider/native-host E2E campaigns.\nNo new typecheck or real-host claim follows from the runtime passes.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Oracle naming scope correction — 2026-10-03\n\nReviewed implementation: [fe40ab59191d046bda12cc9563cdc4a82b5fd97c](https://github.com/TanStack/db/commit/fe40ab59191d046bda12cc9563cdc4a82b5fd97c).\nClassification evidence refers to `134b7e8bacce5999ab7e06da96d5dbe9989820f5`, before the reverse moves.\nThe [classification ledger](2026-10-03-oracle-naming-scope.json) names each evidence path and its line numbers, final path, role, and naming decision.\n\n## Corrected scope\n\nThe earlier claim of 251 executable oracle owners and dedicated companions was too broad.\nThe audit category included ordinary examples, type assertions, harness tests, fixtures, and documentation.\nConverting that category directly into a rename list was incorrect.\nThis record supersedes the naming inventory in [the original review](2026-10-02-glossary-alignment.md).\nIts 39 terminology resolutions remain intact.\n\nThis correction restores 101 original filenames and their imports, commands, replay references, and current documentation links.\nThe PR retains 63 moves: 57 files that execute an independent oracle and six model, grammar, or checker definitions.\nEach retained move has a named mechanism and source evidence in the ledger.\nExisting filenames that already contained `oracle` before this PR remain unchanged.\n\n| Role in the original 251-file review scope | Files |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Executes an independent model, comparison, or generalized checker | 121 |\n| Defines an independent model, checker, or its history grammar | 10 |\n| Ordinary example, regression, or concrete type-assertion tests | 67 |\n| Drivers, fixtures, registration, or supporting declarations | 34 |\n| Harness, checker-calibration, or prototype tests | 17 |\n| Documentation | 2 |\n\nThese are file roles within the previous inventory, not a count of distinct oracles across the repository.\nSeveral files execute the same model, and a mixed test file can contain multiple oracle mechanisms.\nThe classification is conservative for borderline cases. It does not declare all pre-existing oracle names correct.\n\n## Naming evidence\n\nA retained owner executes an independent expected-result computation, state model, differential comparison, metamorphic relation, or reusable law checker.\nA definition owns that model, checker, or its history grammar and names its receiving owner.\nRandom generation is not required. Fixed histories can execute an independent model, as the optimistic settlement histories do.\nOrdinary fixed assertions and parameterization alone are insufficient.\nCoverage-map entries and opening comments do not substitute for executable evidence.\n\nExamples of restored names include `transactions.test.ts`, `query.test-d.ts`, the framework `conformance.test` entrypoints, and `trace-runner.ts`.\nThey contain fixed assertions, registration/driver mechanics, or generic execution plumbing.\nExamples of retained names include `SortedMap-oracle.test.ts`, which compares against native Map plus full sorting,\nand `proxy-oracle.test.ts`, which contains a native-value differential callback model alongside ordinary examples.\nThe test-only no-peek candidate returns to `no-peek.ts`; the independent filter/sort/slice reference remains `model-oracle.ts`.\n\nThe contributor guidance now states this distinction and requires separate counts for owners, definitions, and support.\nIt does not add a CI linter or introduce new product contracts.\n\n## Preservation checks\n\nAn independent content comparison accounted for all 2,164 tracked files before final whitespace formatting.\nIt found 2,048 unchanged blobs, 114 files with mapped path-reference substitutions, and the two naming-policy documents.\nThe correction preserves glossary definitions, identifier/prose fixes, assertions, model rules, and campaign inputs.\nFinal formatting changes only whitespace around shortened paths.\n\nStatic checks found all 101 restored paths and all 251 classified files present and indexed.\nThey checked 672 relative imports, 68 explicit command paths, five browser script entries, and 42 replay targets.\nReplay title selectors remained valid. No stale restored-name references or escaped filename patterns remained in current files.\nHistorical review records and immutable revision links retain their original paths.\n\n## Validation after the correction\n\n| Runtime check | Passed | Files |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| DB | 7,962 | 210 |\n| IVM | 704 | 44 |\n| Offline | 242 | 18 |\n| SQLite core | 375 | 9 |\n| Node SQLite | 109 | 5 |\n| Browser SQLite | 242 | 9 |\n| Electron SQLite | 97 | 3 |\n| Electric | 629 | 13 |\n| Query DB affected no-peek suites | 18 | 2 |\n| React, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Angular receiving suites | 290 | 9 |\n| Total | 10,668 | 322 |\n\nSQLite core also reports one todo. Scoped ESLint passed for 166 changed TypeScript files.\nFormatting and `git diff --check` passed.\nThese runs used the same installed dependencies described in the original record, with coverage and integrated typechecking disabled.\nThe direct command was `node <installed-vitest>/vitest.mjs run --coverage.enabled=false --typecheck.enabled=false --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot`.\nDB used two workers. Framework and Query DB checks selected only the affected receiving files.\n\nThe earlier locked-dependency, integrated-typecheck, and intermittent Query DB baseline limits remain.\nThis correction did not rerun the full Query DB package, package builds, or external-provider/native-host E2E campaigns.\nNo new typecheck or real-host claim follows from the runtime passes.\n"}
